IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ssa-formulas`

-- Social Security Act 1991 (Cth), ss 17(4), 549A, 549C, 1077, 1192-1194, 1203; points 1067G-F28, F31, F35 -- worked cases for
-- ssa-formulas.l4, the amounts computed from the recovered formulas.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were worked by hand from the
-- text and the sidecar formulas, before running. The CPI index numbers, deeming threshold and rates, and the parent's FTB maximum
-- rate are ILLUSTRATIVE inputs chosen by the encoder, not figures in force; the Table G-1 figures are the printed 2017 base figures.

§ `ss 1192-1194, 1203 -- indexation and the assets value limits`

-- 140 / 136 = 1.02941...: 1.029 to 3 places; the 4th place is 4, not greater than 4, so it stays.
#ASSERT `What is the indexation factor` 140 136 EQUALS 1.029
-- 137.5 / 130 = 1.05769...: 1.057, and the 4th place is 6, so s 1193(2) raises it to 1.058.
#ASSERT `What is the indexation factor` 137.5 130 EQUALS 1.058
-- A fall in the CPI: 130 / 135 is below 1, so s 1193(3) makes it 1.
#ASSERT `What is the indexation factor` 130 135 EQUALS 1

-- $250,000 x 1.029 = $257,250, a multiple of $250 (s 1194(1)).
#ASSERT `What is the indexed amount` 250000 1.029 250 EQUALS 257250
-- $187,500 x 1.029 = $192,937.50, nearest $250 is $193,000 (s 1194(2)).
#ASSERT `What is the indexed amount` 187500 1.029 250 EQUALS 193000
-- $287,500 x 1.029 = $295,837.50, nearest $250 is $295,750.
#ASSERT `What is the indexed amount` 287500 1.029 250 EQUALS 295750
-- $1,000 x 1.125 = $1,125, exactly half way: rounded up to $1,250 (s 1194(3)).
#ASSERT `What is the indexed amount` 1000 1.125 250 EQUALS 1250

-- s 1203 on the Table G-1 base figures: $250,000 + 2 x ($287,500 - $187,500) = $450,000, the printed fourth figure.
#ASSERT `What is the single non-homeowner AVL` 250000 287500 187500 EQUALS 450000

-- One indexation from the base figures at 140 / 136: single non-homeowner $257,250 + 2 x ($295,750 - $193,000) = $462,750.
#ASSERT `What is my indexed pension assets value limit` FALSE FALSE 250000 187500 287500 140 136 EQUALS 462750
#ASSERT `What is my indexed pension assets value limit` FALSE TRUE 250000 187500 287500 140 136 EQUALS 257250
#ASSERT `What is my indexed pension assets value limit` TRUE TRUE 250000 187500 287500 140 136 EQUALS 193000
#ASSERT `What is my indexed pension assets value limit` TRUE FALSE 250000 187500 287500 140 136 EQUALS 295750

§ `s 1077 -- deemed income of a member of a pensioner couple`

-- $150,000 against a $100,000 threshold at 0.25% and 2.25%: $250 + $1,125 = $1,375 a year for the couple; each member half,
-- $687.50 a year.
#ASSERT `What yearly income am I deemed to receive` 150000 0 100000 0.0025 0.0225 EQUALS 687.5
-- $80,000 at or below the threshold at 1.3%: $1,040 a year; each member ($1,040 / 52) x 0.5 = $10 a week.
#ASSERT `What weekly income am I deemed to receive` 80000 0 100000 0.013 0.0225 EQUALS 10
-- $80,000 plus $52,000 of home-sale proceeds held under s 1118(2), both at 0.25%: $200 + $130 = $330; each member $165 a year.
#ASSERT `What yearly income am I deemed to receive` 80000 52000 100000 0.0025 0.0225 EQUALS 165

§ `ss 549A, 549C -- youth allowance liquid assets test waiting period`

-- Single, no child, $20,000: ($20,000 - $5,000) / $500 = 30 weeks, capped at 13.
#ASSERT `How many weeks is my youth allowance liquid assets waiting period` 20000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 13
-- $8,000: $3,000 / $500 = 6 weeks.
#ASSERT `How many weeks is my youth allowance liquid assets waiting period` 8000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 6
-- Exactly the $5,000 reserve: not "more than" it, so no waiting period.
#ASSERT `How many weeks is my youth allowance liquid assets waiting period` 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- A member of a couple with $17,500: ($17,500 - $10,000) / $1,000 = 7.5, so 7 whole weeks.
#ASSERT `How many weeks is my youth allowance liquid assets waiting period` 17500 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 7
-- A transferee to youth allowance is not subject to it (s 549A(1)(b)); nor is someone who served one in the last 12 months (2).
#ASSERT `How many weeks is my youth allowance liquid assets waiting period` 20000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How many weeks is my youth allowance liquid assets waiting period` 20000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0

§ `1067G-F28, F31(b), F35 -- parental income test with a relevant sibling`

-- Daniel (d020) at $450 a fortnight, his sister an FTB child of a parent whose FTB maximum rate for her is $6,570 a year:
-- 14/365 x $6,570 = $252, so the F28 total is $450 + $252 = $702.
#ASSERT `What is my F28 total with a relevant sibling` 450 6570 0 EQUALS 702
-- Combined parental income $150,000, free area $55,000: excess $95,000; ($95,000 / 130) x ($450 / $702) = $468.44..., rounded to
-- the nearest 10 cents, $468.40 a fortnight.
#ASSERT `What is my parental income test result with a relevant sibling` 150000 0 55000 FALSE 450 6570 0 EQUALS 468.4
-- Below the free area, or a parent on a Module L payment: nil.
#ASSERT `What is my parental income test result with a relevant sibling` 50000 0 55000 FALSE 450 6570 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is my parental income test result with a relevant sibling` 150000 0 55000 TRUE 450 6570 0 EQUALS 0

§ `s 17(4) -- a lump sum after repaid periodic compensation`

`a $100,000 settlement after $20,000 of periodic compensation` MEANS `My compensation` WITH
    `it is damages, a statutory insurance or compensation scheme payment, a settlement, or another compensation payment` IS TRUE
    `it is made wholly or partly for lost earnings or lost capacity to earn from personal injury` IS TRUE
    `it falls only under paragraph (2)(d) and subsection (2A) takes it out` IS FALSE
    `it is criminal injuries compensation` IS FALSE
    `it is a lump sum` IS TRUE
    `it is only arrears of periodic compensation` IS FALSE
    `the amount` IS 100000
    `it settled a claim related to a disease, injury or condition` IS TRUE
    `it is periodic compensation from a settled claim that I chose to take as a lump sum` IS FALSE
    `the part the Secretary considers is for lost earnings or lost capacity to earn` IS 0
    `maximum basic rate` IS 23000
    `pension supplement component` IS 1800
    `energy supplement component` IS 366
    `ordinary free area limit` IS 1668

-- LSP $100,000 - RPCP $20,000 = $80,000; a settled injury claim, so 50%: $40,000.
#ASSERT `What is the compensation part of my lump sum after repayment` `a $100,000 settlement after $20,000 of periodic compensation` 20000 EQUALS 40000
-- Income cut-out amount [2 x ($23,000 + $1,800 + $366) + $1,668] / 52 = $1,000 a week: $40,000 / $1,000 = 40 weeks.
#ASSERT `How many weeks is my preclusion period after repayment` `a $100,000 settlement after $20,000 of periodic compensation` 20000 EQUALS 40
-- With nothing repaid, the same lump sum gives $50,000 and 50 weeks, as ssa-claims.l4's own cases have it.
#ASSERT `What is the compensation part of my lump sum after repayment` `a $100,000 settlement after $20,000 of periodic compensation` 0 EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT `How many weeks is my preclusion period after repayment` `a $100,000 settlement after $20,000 of periodic compensation` 0 EQUALS 50
